  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14224622/assets/1d8d3dfa1134b7fd5861ff70e493ead2227dd2d322e8436e28a903e0c596a408.png)\n\nConsider the region bounded by the curves $x=4y-{y}^{2},$ $y=\\sqrt{x},$ and the $x$-axis, as shown above. Calculate the volume $V$ of the solid generated when this region is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis. Do not round the answer.\n\n$V=$\n{{field-1}}",
